R&C patch 7118 (DIAGNOSTIC, default off): GCM_PUT_TRACE, a line per guest put store. Applies after 7116 (uses its
put-store hook). Built from the preplan draft-h3-block-built-wrong.patch with the review fixes (review.md s.3). Not
run in a game yet: host test only.

Purpose: hypothesis H3 for the FFA phoenix_ph1 stall (the JUMP-back is never stored at the slot put stops at). The
lifted code says it is [read in code: game-side.md, ppu_recomp_035.cpp l.11382-11394], so H3 is refuted unless a run
shows otherwise; this trace shows it directly, in store order, against the walker's [gcm-putsnap] / FIFO lines. No H3
fix can be written before a run names a wrong store.

What it does: GCM_PUT_TRACE=<n> logs the first n guest put stores (GCM_PUT_TRACE=on or any non-number: 20000; 0: off)
whose old or new put lies in [GCM_PUT_TRACE_LO, GCM_PUT_TRACE_HI) (IO offsets, hex; default all):
`[put-trace] #i put OLD -> NEW get=G w@old=.. w@new-8=.. w@new-4=.. w@new=.. lr=.. tid=..`, words read before the
store lands. Review fixes:
- armed when GCM_PUT_TRACE is set even with GCM_PUT_SNAP=0 (cellGcmInit arms the hook for either; trace only then);
- the default cap is 20000 (the draft's 400 could be spent before the break: 2 in-range stores per injecting frame);
- lr is the guest context's link register = the return of the last lifted call before the store: in FFA 0x006F6138
  0x006F6660 for the forward store (put = slot) and 0x006F6438 for the restore (put = GET) [read in code, review.md
  s.3], not the ~0x6F6AB0 / ~0x6F6440 pcs game-side.md gives.
- with 7116's lifter change the trace works in default runs (no PPU_WWATCH needed).
For FFA: GCM_PUT_TRACE=20000 GCM_PUT_TRACE_LO=00600000 GCM_PUT_TRACE_HI=00700000. H3 test: at the forward store,
w@new must be the JUMP-back 0x2x294944.

Test: port/rc/tests/run_gcm_put_snap_test.sh, mode `trace` (GCM_PUT_SNAP=0 GCM_PUT_TRACE=on: the hook is armed,
nothing is kept, the walker behaves as before, both FFA-shaped stores print with the JUMP-back at w@new).

